# PB0: the BUILD-ONLY job of the window, run BEFORE PA0 while production still serves. C2_ACTIONS=build opens no card, resets nothing and stops nothing: it makes the
# one profile image (the replay-count read-back hook QWEN_FAST_PROFILE_DUMP_EVERY is image code) from the pushed tp4/next-3 commit the window sits on. The build used to
# run inside P2, with production already down, which cost up to 90 minutes of downtime.
# THE TAG MUST BE FRESH. The build step skips a tag that already exists on the host, so a reused tag would silently serve an old image: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prof-2 is a
# PLACEHOLDER and the driver substitutes one new tag, never used before, in every template of this window after checking it is absent from the host's images.
# The profile image is a GATE image: never place it. Pass: the build log ends with the image tagged. Stop rule: any failure stops the window before production is touched.
# Duration (estimate): 18 min typical, 90 at worst.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-3 profile window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prof-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace
